      "comment": "VoiceOver hint for the Library search remaining bar when Remaining time respects speed is off."
    },
    "Estimate. Remaining time respects speed is on, so each episode is divided by that podcast’s playback speed, or Default speed, never below 0.5. This is not the live session rate and not Volume boost. The Home Continue listening bar sums the visible preview rows only. Those rows are in-progress episodes that are not marked played and already have more than one second of progress, newest last played first (last played time, otherwise the playback updated time, title A–Z when the time matches). Home search, when set, keeps episodes whose title, description, episode private note, or bookmark note matches, or whose feed title matches. It does not search chapters or transcripts. Then it keeps at most the first %lld rows. When more episodes match, this is not the full continue-listening catalog. It does not follow the History sort or the History podcast filter, and it is not the History list. The continue catalog comes from the stored History set, which already follows the History size limit, and this bar does not bring trimmed episodes back. Archiving does not by itself remove an in-progress episode from this preview. Played episodes that are not currently playing count as zero. Unknown durations are left out and no time is invented. The episode that is playing uses the live position, but the divisor stays the podcast or default speed. This is not the Library search remaining bar, the Feed remaining bar, the Archived remaining bar, the Downloads remaining bar, the History remaining bar, the Favorites remaining bar, the All Episodes remaining bar, the Queue remaining bar, the Inbox remaining bar, the Subscriptions unplayed remaining bar, the Home New or Inbox preview, the Home Queue preview, the Home History preview, the Home Archived preview, the Home Favorites preview, the Home Downloads preview, the mini player, or Lock Screen. It does not play, download, or mark episodes played.": {
