      "comment": "VoiceOver hint for the Home Favorites remaining bar when Remaining time respects speed is off."
    },
    "Estimate. Remaining time respects speed is on, so each episode is divided by that podcast’s playback speed, or Default speed, never below 0.5. This is not the live session rate and not Volume boost. The Home Downloads bar sums the visible preview rows only. Those rows are completed downloads, newest completed first (download completion time, otherwise the publication date; episode id when the time matches). An episode with neither time comes last. It does not follow the Downloads played-status chip (All, Unplayed, or Played), the Downloads podcast filter, or the Downloads sort, and it is not the Downloads list. Home search, when set, keeps episodes whose title, description, episode private note, or bookmark note matches, or whose feed title matches. It does not search chapters or transcripts. Then it keeps at most the first %lld rows. When more episodes match, this is not the full Downloads list, not the Downloads tab, and not the Downloads tab badge. It is not the full offline Downloads catalog behind Play random, Add all to queue, Add all unplayed to queue, Mark all as played, Mark all as unplayed, Archive all, Cancel all downloads, Delete played downloads, Delete all downloads, Copy downloads, or Share downloads. In-progress downloads are not in this preview. Played episodes that are not currently playing count as zero. Unknown durations are left out and no time is invented. The episode that is playing uses the live position, but the divisor stays the podcast or default speed. This is not the Home Continue listening preview, the Home New or Inbox preview, the Home Queue preview, the Home History preview, the Home Archived preview, the Home Favorites preview, the Library search remaining bar, the Feed remaining bar, the Archived remaining bar, the Downloads remaining bar, the History remaining bar, the Favorites remaining bar, the All Episodes remaining bar, the Queue remaining bar, the Inbox remaining bar, the Subscriptions unplayed remaining bar, the mini player, or Lock Screen. It does not play, download, or mark episodes played.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Estimate. Remaining time respects speed is on, so each episode is divided by that podcast’s playback speed, or Default speed, never below 0.5. This is not the live session rate and not Volume boost. The Home Downloads bar sums the visible preview rows only. Those rows are completed downloads, newest completed first (download completion time, otherwise the publication date; episode id when the time matches). An episode with neither time comes last. It does not follow the Downloads played-status chip (All, Unplayed, or Played), the Downloads podcast filter, or the Downloads sort, and it is not the Downloads list. Home search, when set, keeps episodes whose title, description, episode private note, or bookmark note matches, or whose feed title matches. It does not search chapters or transcripts. Then it keeps at most the first %lld rows. When more episodes match, this is not the full Downloads list, not the Downloads tab, and not the Downloads tab badge. It is not the full offline Downloads catalog behind Play random, Add all to queue, Add all unplayed to queue, Mark all as played, Mark all as unplayed, Archive all, Cancel all downloads, Delete played downloads, Delete all downloads, Copy downloads, or Share downloads. In-progress downloads are not in this preview. Played episodes that are not currently playing count as zero. Unknown durations are left out and no time is invented. The episode that is playing uses the live position, but the divisor stays the podcast or default speed. This is not the Home Continue listening preview, the Home New or Inbox preview, the Home Queue preview, the Home History preview, the Home Archived preview, the Home Favorites preview, the Library search remaining bar, the Feed remaining bar, the Archived remaining bar, the Downloads remaining bar, the History remaining bar, the Favorites remaining bar, the All Episodes remaining bar, the Queue remaining bar, the Inbox remaining bar, the Subscriptions unplayed remaining bar, the mini player, or Lock Screen. It does not play, download, or mark episodes played."
          }
        },
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Schätzung. Verbleibende Zeit berücksichtigt Tempo ist an, daher wird jede Episode durch die Wiedergabegeschwindigkeit dieses Podcasts geteilt, oder durch die Standardgeschwindigkeit, nie unter 0,5. Das ist nicht die Live-Sitzungsrate und nicht die Lautstärke-Verstärkung. Die Home-Downloads-Leiste summiert nur die sichtbaren Vorschauzeilen. Das sind abgeschlossene Downloads, neueste abgeschlossene zuerst (Abschlusszeit des Downloads, sonst das Veröffentlichungsdatum; Episoden-ID bei gleicher Zeit). Eine Episode ohne beide Zeiten kommt zuletzt. Die Leiste folgt nicht dem Downloads-Status-Chip (Alle, Ungehört oder Gehört), dem Downloads-Podcastfilter oder der Downloads-Sortierung und ist nicht die Downloads-Liste. Die Home-Suche behält, wenn sie gesetzt ist, Episoden, deren Titel, Beschreibung, private Episoden-Notiz oder Lesezeichen-Notiz passt, oder deren Feed-Titel passt. Kapitel oder Transkripte werden nicht durchsucht. Danach bleiben höchstens die ersten %lld Zeilen. Wenn mehr Episoden passen, ist das nicht die gesamte Downloads-Liste, nicht der Downloads-Tab und nicht das Downloads-Tab-Badge. Das ist nicht der volle Offline-Downloads-Katalog hinter Zufällig abspielen, Alle zur Warteschlange hinzufügen, Alle ungehörten zur Warteschlange hinzufügen, Alle als gehört markieren, Alle als ungehört markieren, Alle archivieren, Alle Downloads abbrechen, Gehörte Downloads löschen, Alle Downloads löschen, Downloads kopieren oder Downloads teilen. Laufende Downloads sind nicht in dieser Vorschau. Gehörte Episoden, die nicht gerade spielen, zählen als null. Unbekannte Dauern bleiben außen vor und es wird keine Zeit erfunden. Die gerade spielende Episode nutzt die Live-Position, der Teiler bleibt aber die Podcast- oder Standardgeschwindigkeit. Das ist nicht die Home-Weiterhören-Vorschau, die Home-Vorschau Neu oder Posteingang, die Home-Warteschlangen-Vorschau, die Home-Verlauf-Vorschau, die Home-Archiv-Vorschau, die Home-Favoriten-Vorschau, die Bibliothe